Corrected the claim that a GenericSetup export omits provider secrets. It carries them as their stored values, and the `plone.registry.field.Password` type marks a record rather than encrypting it — so an export of a provider is a credential, not a document. The statement appeared eight times, including in the threat model, where the leak was listed as prevented, and in the security guarantees table. What limits exposure is who may take an export, which needs `Manage portal`. @ericof
